<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Alsace</h1><p class="st-meta">640 CE – 740 CE (approx.) · capital Obernai</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Frankish frontier duchy between the Vosges and the Rhine, ruled by the Etichonid family whose saint, Odile, is the patron of Alsace.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the mid 7th century the Merovingian kings of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/austrasia">Austrasia</a> set up a duchy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> to control the border with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alemanni">Alemanni</a>. The first known duke was Gundoin, and from around 662 power passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adalrich-duke-of-alsace">Adalric</a>, also called Eticho, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etichonids">Etichonid</a> dynasty.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes governed from their estates around <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-obernai">Obernai</a> and founded many monasteries. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adalrich-duke-of-alsace">Adalric</a>'s daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-odile">Odile</a> founded the convent of Hohenburg on the mountain now called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mont-sainte-odile">Mont Sainte-Odile</a>, and his descendants endowed abbeys such as Honau and Murbach.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 740, after the death of Duke Liutfrid, the Carolingian mayors abolished the duchy, which had grown too independent, and divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> into two counties, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nordgau">Nordgau</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundgau">Sundgau</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etichonids">Etichonid</a> family remained powerful and gave rise to several later noble houses.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="duchy, 640 CE – 740 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/>